{{Trail|Linguistics}}__NOTOC__
[[Lore:Nordic|Nordic]] was the language spoken by the [[Lore:Nord|Nords]].{{ref|name=BtAoM|{{Cite Book|Before the Ages of Man}}}} It is sometimes referred to as '''Old Nord'''{{ref|{{Cite book|Together Stew Recipe|ns_base=ON}}}} or the '''northern tongue''', referring to [[Lore:Skyrim|Skyrim]].{{ref|name=TIC|{{Cite Book|The Infernal City|ns_base=Books}}}}{{rp|22}} The Nordic god [[Lore:Jhunal|Jhunal]] is considered the father of languages.{{ref|name=VOF|{{Cite Book|Varieties of Faith...}}}}

Nordic first saw use in the [[Lore:Merethic Era#Late Merethic Era|Late Merethic Era]].{{ref|name=TDW}}{{ref|name=Sabatons}} It was considered an old tongue by [[Lore:Second Era|Second Era]],{{ref|name=EGTS}} but saw limited use into even the [[Lore:Fourth Era|Fourth]].{{ref|name=TIC}}{{rp|22}} Next to nothing was known of Atmoran by the Second Era, with instances of the language being increasingly hard to find.{{ref|name=HMTWM}}

==Language Family and Genetic Relationship==
The original [[Lore:Atmora|Atmoran]] tongue likely descended from [[Lore:Ehlnofex|Ehlnofex]], with both tongues using the term [[Lore:Talos|Talos]],{{ref|name=PGE1C}} and was entirely oral, bearing no written form until the Late Merethic Era. [[Lore:Ysgramor|Ysgramor]], considered the first [[Lore:Man|human]] historian, created the runic alphabet of Atmoran speech using the principles of [[Lore:Aldmeris (language)|Elvish]].{{ref|name=BtAoM}}{{ref|name=HMTWM}} When the [[Lore:Dragon Cult|Dragon Cult]] established its firm grip and dominion over Skyrim, [[Lore:Dragon Language|Dragon-tongue]] became the dominant language. Use of the tongue was regulated by the ruling [[Lore:Dragon Priest|Dragon Priests]], who prevented the usage of certain words.{{ref|name=TDW|{{Cite Book|The Dragon War}}}} Nords copied the [[Lore:Dragon Alphabet|Dragon alphabet]] after watching the [[Lore:Dragon|Dragons]] themselves carve the runes with their claws. They used this script for works of importance, such as burials,{{ref|name=DLMnM|{{Cite Book|Dragon Language: Myth no More}}}} but used a lettering system, colloquially referred to as ancient Nord, for other, common purposes.{{ref|name=Nurnhilde|[[ON:Queen Nurnhilde|Queen Nurnhilde]]'s dialogue during [[ON:Sleep for the Dead|Sleep for the Dead]] in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=Sleep|[[ESO:Sleep for the Dead|Sleep for the Dead]] quest in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=Draugr|[[SR:Draugr|Draugr]] dialogue in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} Nordic likely descends from the Atmoran tongue, with the two languages sharing some words.{{ref|name=PGE1C}}{{ref|name=TAH}} It developed around the same time as the ancient Nord variation of Dragon-tongue, as words for Dragon from both languages were used around the same time.{{ref|name=TDW}}

