==Notes==
*{{LNote|nb1|^1.|According to a fan named Athelas, who is a scholar and educator of the real world languages [[Wikipedia:Old English|Old English]] and [[Wikipedia:Old Norse|Old Norse]], the Nordic rune script borrows from the real world [[Wikipedia:Elder Futhark|Elder Futhark]] script, and can be translated to English roughly as: ''"And (the) Ash of the [[Lore:Wulfharth|Wulf]], they recognize that doom."'' The script then repeats two additional times.{{ref|name=Runestone|group=LANG|1=[https://web.archive.org/web/20230316073313/https://www.imperial-library.info/content/nordic-runes-eso#comment-27963 ''Translating the Bleakrock Runeston Introduction and Translation]''}}}}
*{{LNote|nb2|^2.|According to Athelas, this rune script can be translated to English roughly as: ''"[[Lore:Ysgramor|Ysgramor]] (went) forth higher and they rowed inwards up : Ysgramor they made a pull of the oar; they recognize that doom."''{{ref|name=Runestone|group=LANG}}}}
*{{LNote|nb3|^3.|These wall textures feature the Elder Futhark script (later used as Nordic script for [[Online:Online|ESO]]) and are found scattered throughout the Fortress of Ice, the home of the [[Lore:Shalidor|Archmagus Shalidor]], who was a Nord.{{Ref|name=RiaSilmane|Dialogue with [[Arena:Ria Silmane|Ria Silmane]] in ''[[Arena:Arena|Arena]]''}}{{ref|name=AMM|{{Cite Book|A Minor Maze}}}}{{Ref|name=Shalidor|[[Online:Arch-Mage Shalidor|Arch-Mage Shalidor]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}}}
*{{LNote|nb4|^4.|These sprites also feature the Elder Futhark script (later used as Nordic script for ESO) and are used often throughout the entire game world of [[Arena:Arena|''Arena'']].}}

